1851,4903],[1821,4903],[1878,4902],[1854,4901],[1825,4901],[1941,4900],[2324,4899],[2080,4898],[1942,4897],[1881,4896],[1266,4895],[1262,4894],[1759,4893],[1615,4893],[2325,4892],[1742,4891],[1598,4891],[1850,4890],[1820,4889],[2327,4888],[1761,4887],[1617,4887],[1852,4886],[1822,4886],[1879,4885],[2272,4884],[2271,4883],[2273,4882],[2048,4881],[2045,4881],[2050,4880],[2049,4879],[2052,4878],[2051,4877],[2046,4876],[2053,4875],[2047,4874],[2328,4873],[2084,4872],"What it does Sections Short example PHP library for the Shikimori GraphQL API (`shikimori.io`). The package `devcraftclub/shikimori-api-php` returns typed objects, limits request frequency, and can store responses in a file cache or in a database through Cycle ORM. PHP 8.3 and newer, strict types `ShikimoriClient` facade and repositories for each catalog section List filters composed with a `with*` chain Two GraphQL field profiles: short and detailed File cache by default, Cycle ORM when you ask for it OAuth2 for requests on behalf of a user Limit of 5 requests per second and 90 per minute Composer and environment variables Anime, manga, and field profiles Authorization URL and code exchange Cache, database, and a fresh request Package classes Russian documentation","What it does Sections Short example PHP library for the official MyShows JSON-RPC API (`https://api.myshows.me/v2/rpc/`). The package `devcraftclub/myshows-api-php` calls methods by API section and returns typed objects. The package `composer.json` does not set a version field yet. This documentation treats the first documented release as `1.0.0`. PHP 8.3 and newer `MyShowsClient` facade and repositories for each API section Public methods without sign-in and private methods through OAuth2 File cache for responses by default Token file storage and access token refresh Request rate limiting Separate exceptions for network, JSON-RPC, sign-in, and rate limit Composer and environment variables Show card, search, and episodes Authorization code, profile, and episode check-in Reuse without the network and force refresh Package classes Russian documentation","Values **Description:** Fixed set of values. **Namespace:** `DevCraftClub\\Shikimori\\Query` **Since:** 1.0.0 Name Value `Summary` `'summary'` `Detail` `'detail'`","Values **Description:** Fixed set of values. **Namespace:** `DevCraftClub\\Shikimori\\Enum` **Since:** 1.0.0 Name Value `Tv` `'tv'` `Movie` `'movie'` `Ova` `'ova'` `Ona` `'ona'` `Special` `'special'` `Music` `'music'` `TvSpecial` `'tv_special'` `None` `'none'`","Values **Description:** Fixed set of values. **Namespace:** `DevCraftClub\\Shikimori\\Enum` **Since:** 1.0.0 Name Value `Planned` `'planned'` `Watching` `'watching'` `Rewatching` `'rewatching'` `Completed` `'completed'` `OnHold` `'on_hold'` `Dropped` `'dropped'`","Values **Description:** Fixed set of values. **Namespace:** `DevCraftClub\\Shikimori\\Enum` **Since:** 1.0.0 Name Value `None` `'none'` `G` `'g'` `Pg` `'pg'` `Pg13` `'pg_13'` `R` `'r'` `RPlus` `'r_plus'` `Rx` `'rx'`","Values **Description:** Fixed set of values. **Namespace:** `DevCraftClub\\Shikimori\\Enum` **Since:** 1.0.0 Name Value `Id` `'id'` `Ranked` `'ranked'` `Kind` `'kind'` `Popularity` `'popularity'` `Name` `'name'` `AiredOn` `'aired_on'` `Episodes` `'episodes'` `Status` `'status'`","Values **Description:** Fixed set of values. **Namespace:** `DevCraftClub\\Shikimori\\Enum` **Since:** 1.0.0 Name Value `Id` `'id'` `Ranked` `'ranked'` `Kind` `'kind'` `Popularity` `'popularity'` `Name` `'name'` `AiredOn` `'aired_on'` `CreatedAt` `'created_at'` `UpdatedAt` `'updated_at'`","Values **Description:** Fixed set of values. **Namespace:** `DevCraftClub\\Shikimori\\Enum` **Since:** 1.0.0 Name Value `Anons` `'anons'` `Ongoing` `'ongoing'` `Released` `'released'`","Values **Description:** Fixed set of values. **Namespace:** `DevCraftClub\\Shikimori\\Enum` **Since:** 1.0.0 Name Value `Anime` `'Anime'` `Manga` `'Manga'`","Values **Description:** Fixed set of values. **Namespace:** `DevCraftClub\\MyShows\\Enum` **Since:** 1.0.0 Name Value `Watching` `'watching'` `Later` `'later'` `Completed` `'completed'` `Cancelled` `'cancelled'` `OnHold` `'onhold'`","Values **Description:** Fixed set of values. **Namespace:** `DevCraftClub\\MyShows\\Enum` **Since:** 1.0.0 **See also:** Object UserShowStatus Name Value `Watching` `'watching'` `Later` `'later'` `Cancelled` `'cancelled'` `Remove` `'remove'`","Values **Description:** Fixed set of values. **Namespace:** `DevCraftClub\\MyShows\\Enum` **Since:** 1.0.0 **See also:** Object UserEpisodeStatus Name Value `Watched` `'watched'` `Unwatched` `'unwatched'` `Ignored` `'ignored'`","ValidationRule contract Attributes `Filter` `Range` `Regex` `ArrayOf` PropertyValidator ValidationException Validation rules are PHP attributes that implement `Devcraft\\Interfaces\\ValidationRule`. They return `null` when valid, or a short message when invalid. `null` input always passes (requiredness is handled by the mapper's null fallback). Messages describe expectation only (`must be numeric`), not the actual value. Paths and actual types are attached by `ReflectionMapper` / `ValidationException`. All validation attributes target properties and are repeatable. Wraps PHP's `filter_var`: `FILTER_VALIDATE_BOOLEAN` automatically adds `FILTER_NULL_ON_FAILURE` so invalid booleans are rejected instead of coerced to `false`. Failure message: `must pass filter {id}`. Numeric bounds for `int` or `float` values: Either bound may be omitted. Non-numeric values fail with `must be numeric`. String pattern match: The constructor validates the pattern with `preg_match` and throws `InvalidArgumentException` if the expression is invalid. Non-string values fail with `must be a string`. Ensures the value is a list whose elements match a type name: Supported builtins: `mixed`, `string`, `int`/`integer`, `float`/`double`, `bool`/`boolean`, `array`, `object`. Other names are treated as class/interface checks via `instanceof`. In `ReflectionMapper`, `ArrayOf` also drives nested conversion before validation runs. `Devcraft\\Validation\\PropertyValidator` runs attribute rules without hydration: `validateObject()` inspects only public, non-static, initialized properties. Non-`ValidationRule` attributes are ignored. Multiple rules on one property contribute multiple messages. Thrown by `ReflectionMapper` when one or more required property paths fail: `getErrors()` returns `array<string, list<string>>` keyed by dotted property paths.","ValidationRule contract Attributes `Filter` `Range` `Regex` `ArrayOf` PropertyValidator ValidationException Related Validation rules are PHP attributes that implement `Devcraft\\Interfaces\\ValidationRule`. They return `null` when valid, or a short message when invalid. `null` input always passes (requiredness is handled by the mapper's null fallback). Messages describe expectation only (`must be numeric`), not the actual value. Paths and actual types are attached by `ReflectionMapper` / `ValidationException`. All validation attributes target properties and are repeatable. Wraps PHP's `filter_var`: `FILTER_VALIDATE_BOOLEAN` automatically adds `FILTER_NULL_ON_FAILURE` so invalid booleans are rejected instead of coerced to `false`. Failure message: `must pass filter <id>`. Numeric bounds for `int` or `float` values: Either bound may be omitted. Non-numeric values fail with `must be numeric`. String pattern match: The constructor validates the pattern with `preg_match` and throws `InvalidArgumentException` if the expression is invalid. Non-string values fail with `must be a string`. Ensures the value is a list whose elements match a type name: Supported builtins: `mixed`, `string`, `int`/`integer`, `float`/`double`, `bool`/`boolean`, `array`, `object`. Other names are treated as class/interface checks via `instanceof`. In `ReflectionMapper`, `ArrayOf` also drives nested conversion before validation runs. `Devcraft\\Validation\\PropertyValidator` runs attribute rules without hydration: `validateObject()` inspects only public, non-static, initialized properties. Non-`ValidationRule` attributes are ignored. Multiple rules on one property contribute multiple messages. Thrown by `ReflectionMapper` when one or more required property paths fail: `getErrors()` returns `array<string, list<string>>` keyed by dotted property paths. ValidationRule PropertyValidator ValidationException API reference Changelog","Update-policy (host DLE + DevCraft) Install и базовые команды: инструкция Graphify. Пути `graphify update .` `engine/**` (не cache), `templates/Default/**`, `language/Russian/**` Да `devcraft/src/**`, `devcraft/config/**`, `devcraft/locales/**`, `devcraft/*.php` Да Только docs / `.cursor` Нет Ignore: `.graphifyignore` (`devcraft/` с исключениями `!src` / `!config` / `!locales` / `!*.php`). Правило Cursor: `.cursor/rules/graphify.mdc`.","The cache directory is `MYSHOWS_CACHE_DIR`. Entry lifetime is `MYSHOWS_CACHE_TTL` in seconds. A normal call checks the stored copy first. If the network is down and a copy exists, the method returns it. `forceRecheck: true` skips the copy. Without a network such a call throws `NetworkException`. Methods that change user data clear related cache entries so the next show card does not show a stale check-in.","System requirements Installation methods Verify Troubleshooting Next Item Minimum PHP **8.3+** Composer yes `psr/cache` `^3.0` (pulled in automatically) `marcin-orlowski/lombok-php` `^1.2` (for `get*` / `set*` on `AbstractWith`) No separate config file: after `composer require`, the `Devcraft\\` namespaces come from `vendor` autoload. Composer also installs lombok-php and `psr/cache`. On sites with DevCraft Admin the package is already a dependency of the shell — add it yourself only for standalone PHP projects. Path repositories belong in the consuming project's **root** `composer.json`. Nested packages do not inherit them. Then: Point `url` at a local clone. Use `^1.1` or `@dev` while developing; switch to Packagist/VCS later. Expect `1.1.0` (or compatible `^1.1`) and PHP `>=8.3`. For cache usage, `psr/cache` must appear in the dependency tree. Declare path repositories only in the consumer root `composer.json`. Requires PHP 8.3+. Check `php -v` and Composer `config.platform`. Need package version **≥ 1.1.0** and an installed `psr/cache`. Getting started PSR-6 file cache With attributes","System requirements Installation methods Configuration Verify the install Troubleshooting PHP 8.3 or newer Composer Transitive runtime: `marcin-orlowski/lombok-php` `^1.2` (installed with the package) Composer also installs `marcin-orlowski/lombok-php` `^1.2`. `AbstractWith` extends `\\Lombok\\Helper`. Path repositories belong in the consuming project's root `composer.json`. Composer does not inherit them transitively. Then: Set `url` to the relative or absolute path of the package on disk. Later you can switch the path repository to a VCS/Packagist source and a version constraint. No extra config file is required. After Composer resolves the package, autoload `Devcraft\\\\` namespaces from `vendor`. Expected: version `1.0.1` and PHP `>=8.3`. Path repositories must be declared in the **root** consumer `composer.json`. Nested packages cannot inherit them. The package requires PHP 8.3 or newer. Check `php -v` and the platform config in Composer.","Skill — инструкция `SKILL.md`, которую агент читает **до** кода. Кладите project skills в `.cursor/skills/{name}/` (или personal `~/.cursor/skills/`). На страницах ниже — **полное содержимое** skill (не краткое описание). Краткий каталог: Справочник ИИ. Skill Что внутри using-superpowers Правило вызова, приоритет, красные флаги grill-with-docs grilling + domain-modeling целиком create-devcraft-plugin Интервью, канон дерева, чеклист caveman Уровни речи, границы, отличие от MCP codebase-memory Матрица tools, трасса, Cypher, ловушки","Show card Search Top, genres, and one episode `withEpisodes: true` asks for the episode list together with the show. A repeat call with the same arguments reads the file cache until `MYSHOWS_CACHE_TTL` expires.","Setup / auth Когда Полная установка: инструкция mem0. Ключ на app.mem0.ai/dashboard/api-keys. Cursor Desktop: Environment → Local → `MEM0_API_KEY=m0-…` (или reinstall plugin с prompt). CLI: `export MEM0_API_KEY=…` в `~/.zshrc` / `~/.bashrc`. После ключа — `mem0:onboard`, если skill доступен. `auth=none` → не вызывать add/search; настроить ключ. **Не коммитить** ключ в git. Кросс-сессионные предпочтения команды (язык PHPDoc, AJAX only `devcraft/ajax.php`). Не секреты. Не граф кода. Правило: `.cursor/rules/mem0.mdc`.","Setup / auth (MUST) Ссылки Установка Использование Пример на DevCraft См. также **mem0** (mem0ai/mem0) — production memory layer для агентов: Python/Node SDK, cloud platform или self-host. В Cursor MCP часто фигурирует как `user-mem0` с tools `add_memory`, `search_memories`, `get_memories` и др. **mem0** ≠ cavemem (локальный SQLite сессий) ≠ memory (локальный entity graph) ≠ codebase-memory-mcp (граф **кода**). Ключ: app.mem0.ai/dashboard/api-keys → `MEM0_API_KEY` вида `m0-…`. **Cursor Desktop:** environment рядом с prompt → Local → gear → `MEM0_API_KEY=m0-…`. Либо переустановить mem0-плагин — IDE запросит ключ (keychain). **CLI / shell:** `export MEM0_API_KEY=m0-…` в `~/.zshrc` / `~/.bashrc`. После появления ключа — skill &#x2A;*`mem0:onboard`** (если доступен в окружении). Статус хука `auth=none` → **не** вызывать write/search так, будто память работает; сначала setup. **Не коммитить** API key в git / docs / `.env` репозитория. Репозиторий: mem0ai/mem0 Upstream docs: docs.mem0.ai Контекст DevCraft: development\\_help/mcp/mem0 Hosted API + MCP-плагин IDE — типичный путь. Self-host / SDK — по README upstream (`mem0ai` / `@mem0/oss`). Без ключа tools бесполезны. Операция Назначение `add_memory` Записать предпочтение / решение команды `search_memories` Найти факты перед задачей `get_memories` / update / delete Жизненный цикл записей **Когда:** кросс-сессионные предпочтения (язык PHPDoc, запрет `devcraft/bin`, стек DLE 20 + DevCraft 200.4) на нескольких машинах через platform. **Не нужно:** секреты; пароли; дублировать граф кода (туда — Codebase Memory / CRG / graphify). `add_memory`: «Команда DevCraft: UI/PHPDoc/ошибки на русском; AJAX только через `devcraft/ajax.php`; нет standalone CLI». Перед миграцией модуля — `search_memories` по «DevCraft conventions». cavemem memory (MCP) Справочник ИИ Cursor-rule: `.cursor/rules/mem0.mdc` (host)","Scope Стек Принципы (MUST) Оверлей DevCraft Review gates Graphify См. также Публичный дайджест правил PHP-разработки модулей DevCraft (и совместимого legacy MH Admin). **Иерархия при конфликте:** Конституция > Roistat PHP Code Conventions > legacy `mhadmin`. Входит Не входит (явно исключено) Семантика PHP (Roistat Code Conv) Правила PR-workflow Стиль форматирования (Principle VIII) Обязательные тесты / test env Стек, слои, DLE/DevCraft интеграция Standalone CLI (`bin/`) Документация без явного запроса Слой Технология Runtime PHP **≥ 8.3** Шаблоны Twig Persistence Cycle ORM Admin UI Metro UI Хост DLE **20.0** Workspace репозиторий/проект модуля на DevCraft Legacy-референс проект `mhadmin` и его `graphify-out/` (если есть) # Принцип Кратко I Roistat semantics Читаемость, без мёртвого кода, typed/IDE-refactorable; narrative comments не раздувать (`// hack:`, `@todo` — ок) II Слои Service / Repository / Controller / Entity / DTO — без cross-layer shortcuts III PHP 8.3 typing Типы везде; `validate*`/`check*` бросают; getters без префикса `get` IV Cycle ORM Нет ad-hoc SQL в контроллерах/сервисах (кроме миграций) V Twig HTML только через Twig; данные готовятся в PHP VI Metro UI Паттерны из примеров Metro UI, без параллельных CSS-фреймворков VII DRY Одна точка истины для повторяющейся логики VIII Code style Tabs, margin 150, вертикальное выравнивание `=`/`=>`, braces on new line IX DLE 20 `DLEPlugins::Check()`, prefix, topics 72–75; &#x2A;*DevCraft:** AJAX только через `devcraft/ajax.php` X No CLI Нет `devcraft/bin` и shell entry points XI No unsolicited docs README/docs только по явному запросу Комментарии, PHPDoc и UI/ошибки в PHP — **на русском**. Это не отменяет запрет на «воду» в комментариях (I). Принципы I–XI Roistat digest для затронутого кода Style profile (VIII) Cycle + Twig + Metro для новых частей Нет нового CLI / unsolicited docs Граф Роль `graphify-out/` у legacy `mhadmin` PRIMARY для старой раскладки модулей `graphify-out/` у host DLE Состояние хоста; `graphify update .` после правок `engine/` (не после чистого `devcraft/`) Начало работы PHP DevCraft Standards ИИ-инструменты Точки входа","Requirements Installation Packagist Local path repository Choosing a base class Architecture Use case A — Fluent builder Use case B — API response DTO Running tests in this package Next steps This guide walks through installing DevCraft Dev Tools, choosing the right base class, and building a first fluent builder and a first response DTO. PHP 8.3 or newer Composer A consuming project that can declare a Composer path repository (or a published package version). Path repositories must be configured by the consuming root project. Composer does not inherit them transitively. Then: Adjust `url` to the relative or absolute path of this package on disk. Publish this package later, or replace the path repository with a normal VCS/Packagist repository and a version constraint. Need Extend Property style Fluent builders / query objects `AbstractWith` Private (or protected), non-static, non-readonly API response / request DTOs `AbstractReflection` Public, typed, hydratable Do **not** combine them through inheritance. Private fluent properties and public mapped properties solve different problems. If a type needs both shapes, prefer composition or two separate classes. A real-world fluent example is a WebShare-style query builder: chain `withPage()`, `withPageSize()`, and filter helpers, then render a query string. That pattern maps cleanly onto `AbstractWith` plus `#[With]` / `#[WithItem]`. Extend `AbstractWith` and annotate private properties: How it works: `AbstractWith::__call()` forwards unknown methods to `WithHandler`. `#[With]` creates `withPropertyName($value)` and replaces the whole property. `#[WithItem]` creates `withPropertyNameItem(...)`. One type descriptor means append; two descriptors mean map set. Methods return `$this`, so chaining is the normal style. See With attributes for property constraints, naming rules, unions, and error types. Extend `AbstractReflection` and declare public typed properties, optionally with validation attributes: How it works: `fromArray()` creates an instance and hydrates public properties through `ReflectionMapper`. Scalars may be coerced from strings where safe (`\"8080\"` → `8080`, `\"false\"` → `false`). Nested classes that extend `AbstractReflection` are hydrated recursively. `#[ArrayOf]` maps list elements to a declared type. Validation attributes run after conversion; failures raise `ValidationException`. See Reflection mapper and Validation for details. From the DevTool repository root: `composer test` runs PHPUnit via `phpunit.xml.dist`, which bootstraps `vendor/autoload.php` and discovers everything under `tests/`. Read With attributes if you are building fluent APIs. Read Reflection mapper if you are mapping API payloads. Read Validation to attach `Filter`, `Range`, `Regex`, or `ArrayOf` rules.","Requirements Installation Configuration Quick start Request surface Domain glossary Next PHP wrapper for the WebShare Proxy API with rate-limit retries, GET response caching, filtering, pagination iterators, and typed request helpers. PHP >= 8.3 Composer WebShare API key Or `.env`: `App::Client()` returns the shared HTTP client. `App::Requests('Profile'|'Notification'|…)` auto-discovers request classes. App::Requests key Coverage `Proxy` list, iterate, download, refresh `Profile` profile + preferences `Notification` list/retrieve/dismiss/restore `ProxyReplacement` list/retrieve/create (v3) `ReplacedProxy` list/download `ProxyConfig` config/status/listStats/update (v3) `IpAuthorization` list/iterate/CRUD + whatsMyIp `ProxyStats` list/aggregate/activities/download `DownloadToken` get/reset token by scope `ApiKey` list/iterate/CRUD `SubUser` list/iterate/CRUD/refresh + `masqueradeAs()` **Proxy Connection** is not a REST resource — use `Proxy::getConnectionString()` (backbone/direct). Term Meaning Proxy Single proxy endpoint from a list ProxyList Paginated collection of Proxies ProxyConfig Plan-level proxy configuration IpAuthorization Allowlisted source IP SubUser Child account under the parent plan X-Subuser Header to masquerade as a SubUser DownloadToken Time-limited download key PageIterator Walks paginated pages until `next` is null BackboneConnection / DirectConnection Connection modes via `getConnectionString()` Proxies Auth and tokens SubUsers Stats and config","Requirements Install the package Environment variables Check PHP 8.3, 8.4, or 8.5 The `json` extension Composer Set the application name. Without it, Shikimori may reject the request. The database is needed only when you call `withDatabase()` or `withOrm()`. A filled `title` means the client reached the API.","Requirements Install the package Environment variables Check PHP 8.3 and newer Composer Access to `https://api.myshows.me` Public methods need an application name and a language. Private methods need an OAuth2 application on the MyShows side. A non-empty `title` means the request reached the API.","Quick start Filtering, ordering and search Pagination Download and refresh Connection strings Replacements Work with the proxy list via `App::Requests('Proxy')`, `QueryBuilder` filters, page iteration, and connection strings (backbone / direct). Operator API syntax `EQUAL` `?field=value` `IN` `?field__in=a,b` `GT` / `LT` `?field__gt=` / `__lt=` `CONTAINS` `?field__contains=` Manual pages via `withPage` / `withStartingAfter`, or `iterate()` / `PageIterator::items()` (default max pages from `ITERATE_MAX_PAGES`, default 100). Paths containing `/download/` are never cached. Not a REST resource — use `Proxy::getConnectionString()`: `App::Requests('ProxyReplacement')` — list / retrieve / create (v3) `App::Requests('ReplacedProxy')` — list / download","Quick start Class vs property Naming Constructor Limitations Related `AbstractWith` extends `\\Lombok\\Helper`. `#[Getter]` and `#[Setter]` come from `marcin-orlowski/lombok-php`, not from Dev Tools. This guide covers the integration only. Full attribute contract: lombok-php attributes. `withPage()` goes to WithHandler. `getPage()` / `setVisible()` / `isVisible()` go to Lombok. Put the attributes on the class or on a property. On the **class**: accessors for every eligible property. `public` and `static` are skipped silently. `#[Setter]` also skips `readonly` properties. On a **property**: that property only. `public` / `static` / `readonly` (for Setter) throw. If a property already has `#[Getter]` or `#[Setter]`, the class-level scope is **not** applied to that property. Use that to narrow accessors: `$name` gets `getName()` and `setName()`. `$id` gets `getId()` only. `#[With]` / `#[WithItem]` are not Lombok accessor attributes. Class-level `#[Getter]` coexists with `#[With]` on the same property. Names are StudlyCase of the property: `$starting_after` → `getStartingAfter()` / `setStartingAfter()`. When the property's only type is `bool`, the getter is `isVisible()`, not `getVisible()`. A union that includes `bool` uses plain `get`. `set*` returns `$this` for chaining. Helper calls `Lombok::construct($this)` from `__construct()`. If a subclass declares its own constructor: Without `parent::__construct()`, `with*` still works immediately. Getters and setters attach on the first Lombok `__call` (or not at all until you call `get*` / `set*`). For a `readonly` **class**, lombok requires `\\Lombok\\HelperReadonly`, not `Helper`. `AbstractWith` extends the regular Helper, so readonly classes are out of scope. Readonly **properties** are skipped by class-level Setter. Magic methods cannot satisfy interface methods. IDEs will not see `get*` / `set*` unless you add `@method` PHPDoc. A name collision with a real method: on a property, an exception; on the class, the original method stays and no accessor is added. See also: AbstractWith, With attributes. API reference Changelog","Quick start AbstractWith Property constraints Method naming `#[With]` — replace the whole value `#[WithItem]` — append or map Append (one type descriptor) Map (two type descriptors) Combined with `#[With]` Type descriptors Runtime vs configuration errors Metadata caching Inheritance Use `#[With]` and `#[WithItem]` to generate fluent setters for private (or protected) properties. Extend `AbstractWith` so `__call` routes those virtual methods through `WithHandler`. Canonical builder sample (with getters): `Devcraft\\Abstracts\\AbstractWith` is the recommended base class: You can call `WithHandler` yourself if you need a custom `__call`, but subclasses of `AbstractWith` get the routing for free. Attributes are only valid on properties that are: non-public (private or protected) non-static non-readonly `#[WithItem]` additionally requires a non-nullable `array` property. Invalid configurations throw `LogicException` when metadata is first built (on the first `handles()` / `call()` for that class). Property names are converted to StudlyCase: Property `#[With]` method `#[WithItem]` method `$page` `withPage($value)` — `$starting_after` `withStartingAfter($value)` — `$tags` `withTags($array)` `withTagsItem($item)` `$labels` — `withLabelsItem($key, $value)` Lookup is case-insensitive (`WITHPAGE` works). Method names must remain unique across the inheritance chain; collisions (including case-only collisions such as `$name` / `$NAME`) throw `LogicException`. Expects exactly one argument. Uses PHP's normal property type check (no string→int coercion for typed properties). Returns `$this`. Map keys may only be typed as `int` and/or `string`. Descriptors are strings or lists of strings (unions): Supported builtins: `string`, `int`, `float`, `bool`, `true`, `false`, `null`, `array`, `object`, `iterable`, `callable`, `mixed`. Also supported: class, interface, and enum names that exist at runtime. Notes: `mixed` cannot be combined with other types in the same union. `float` does not accept integers (no numeric coercion). `void` / `never` are rejected. Unknown class names throw `LogicException` at metadata build time. Situation Exception Public / static / readonly property `LogicException` Nullable or non-array `WithItem` target `LogicException` Bad descriptor count / empty union / invalid map key types `LogicException` Repeated attribute / virtual method collision `LogicException` Uninitialized array on append/map `LogicException` Wrong argument count `ArgumentCountError` Value fails descriptor check `TypeError` Unknown virtual method via `WithHandler::call` `BadMethodCallException` Invalid item/map arguments are checked before mutation, so failed calls do not partially update the array. `WithHandler` builds and caches operation metadata per runtime class on first use. Subsequent calls reuse the same writers and property reflections. The cache stores closures bound to the declaring class, not to fixture instances. Attributes on private and protected properties declared in parent classes are discovered and work on child instances. Writers are bound to the declaring class so private parent properties remain writable through the virtual methods.","Quick start AbstractWith Property constraints Method naming `#[With]` — replace the whole value `#[WithItem]` — append or map Append (one type descriptor) Map (two type descriptors) Combined with `#[With]` Type descriptors Runtime vs configuration errors Metadata caching Inheritance Related Use `#[With]` and `#[WithItem]` to generate fluent setters for private (or protected) properties. Extend `AbstractWith`: `__call` sends `with*` to `WithHandler` first, then to `\\Lombok\\Helper` (`get*` / `set*` / `is*`). Canonical builder sample (with `#[Getter]`): See also: Getters and setters. `Devcraft\\Abstracts\\AbstractWith` extends `\\Lombok\\Helper`. It is the recommended base class: `with*` is handled by `WithHandler`. Everything else goes to Lombok. An unknown method raises `BadMethodCallException` from Helper. If a subclass defines `__construct()`, call `parent::__construct()` so getters and setters attach immediately. `with*` methods do not depend on that call. You can call `WithHandler` yourself in a custom `__call`, but then you must forward the rest to Lombok. Attributes are only valid on properties that are: non-public (private or protected) non-static non-readonly `#[WithItem]` additionally requires a non-nullable `array` property. Invalid configurations throw `LogicException` when metadata is first built (on the first `handles()` / `call()` for that class). Property names are converted to StudlyCase: Property `#[With]` method `#[WithItem]` method `$page` `withPage($value)` — `$starting_after` `withStartingAfter($value)` — `$tags` `withTags($array)` `withTagsItem($item)` `$labels` — `withLabelsItem($key, $value)` Lookup is case-insensitive (`WITHPAGE` works). Method names must remain unique across the inheritance chain; collisions (including case-only collisions such as `$name` / `$NAME`) throw `LogicException`. Expects exactly one argument. Uses PHP's normal property type check (no string→int coercion for typed properties). Returns `$this`. Map keys may only be typed as `int` and/or `string`. Descriptors are strings or lists of strings (unions): Supported builtins: `string`, `int`, `float`, `bool`, `true`, `false`, `null`, `array`, `object`, `iterable`, `callable`, `mixed`. Also supported: class, interface, and enum names that exist at runtime. Notes: `mixed` cannot be combined with other types in the same union. `float` does not accept integers (no numeric coercion). `void` / `never` are rejected. Unknown class names throw `LogicException` at metadata build time. Situation Exception Public / static / readonly property `LogicException` Nullable or non-array `WithItem` target `LogicException` Bad descriptor count / empty union / invalid map key types `LogicException` Repeated attribute / virtual method collision `LogicException` Uninitialized array on append/map `LogicException` Wrong argument count `ArgumentCountError` Value fails descriptor check `TypeError` Unknown virtual method via `WithHandler::call` `BadMethodCallException` Invalid item/map arguments are checked before mutation, so failed calls do not partially update the array. `WithHandler` builds and caches operation metadata per runtime class on first use. Subsequent calls reuse the same writers and property reflections. The cache stores closures bound to the declaring class, not to fixture instances. Attributes on private and protected properties declared in parent classes are discovered and work on child instances. Writers are bound to the declaring class so private parent properties remain writable through the virtual methods. AbstractWith With WithItem WithHandler Getters and setters Changelog","Quick start AbstractReflection API Hydration rules Scalar conversion Nested DTOs Null fallback `#[ArrayOf]` Serialization Logging Direct mapper use Related `AbstractReflection` is the base class for DTOs with public typed properties. It exposes `fromArray()`, `toArray()`, and `toJson()`. Hydration and serialization are implemented by `ReflectionMapper`. Canonical Proxy / Address sample: Method Description `static fromArray(array $data): static` Create an instance and hydrate public properties `toArray(): array` Export initialized public properties (nested DTOs recursively) `toJson(): string` Pretty-printed JSON with Unicode and slashes unescaped; throws `JsonException` on failure `static setLogger(LoggerInterface $logger): void` Override the logger used for validation failures `static resetLogger(): void` Clear the custom logger (tests / teardown) Only **public, non-static** properties participate in mapping. Private/protected fields are ignored by the mapper. `ReflectionMapper::hydrate($target, $data)` walks public properties: Missing keys or explicit `null` trigger the null fallback. Values are converted according to the property type. `#[ArrayOf]` post-processes list properties. Validation attributes run on the converted value. Failures are logged and collected; after the pass, a non-empty error map raises `ValidationException`. Declared type Accepted input `string` string only `int` int, or numeric string via `FILTER_VALIDATE_INT` `float` float, int, or numeric string via `FILTER_VALIDATE_FLOAT` `bool` bool, `0`/`1`, or boolean strings via `FILTER_VALIDATE_BOOLEAN` `array` array `object` object `mixed` / untyped anything Union and intersection property types are not supported and fail conversion. If the property type is a subclass of `AbstractReflection` and the input is an array, the mapper instantiates the nested class and hydrates it with a dotted path prefix (`address.city`, `locations.0.city`). If the input is already an instance of the declared type (or interface), it is accepted as-is. When a key is missing or the value is `null`: properties with a default value keep their default nullable properties without a usable value become `null` required non-nullable properties without a default record `is required` When conversion or validation fails for a **nullable** property, the mapper sets the property to `null` instead of adding that path to the thrown error map (the failure is still logged). `ArrayOf` is both a conversion hint for the mapper and a `ValidationRule`. During conversion, the property value must be a **list** (`array_is_list`). Each element is converted to the declared type (builtin or nested `AbstractReflection`). Associative arrays fail with `must be a list`. Element failures appear as `ids.1`, `locations.0.city`, and so on. `toArray()` includes only initialized public properties. Nested `AbstractReflection` instances are expanded recursively. Plain arrays are walked element by element. `toJson()` encodes `toArray()` with: `JSON_THROW_ON_ERROR` `JSON_UNESCAPED_UNICODE` `JSON_PRETTY_PRINT` `JSON_UNESCAPED_SLASHES` `JSON_INVALID_UTF8_SUBSTITUTE` By default `AbstractReflection` uses an `Analog\\Logger`. Call `setLogger()` to capture validation failures in tests or application logging: Each failure is logged at error level with context keys `class`, `property` (dotted path), `expected`, and `actual_type`. You can hydrate an existing object without `fromArray()`: An optional second constructor argument accepts a custom `PropertyValidator`. AbstractReflection ReflectionMapper ArrayOf Validation Changelog","Quick start AbstractReflection API Hydration rules Scalar conversion Nested DTOs Null fallback `#[ArrayOf]` Serialization Logging Direct mapper use `AbstractReflection` is the base class for DTOs with public typed properties. It exposes `fromArray()`, `toArray()`, and `toJson()`. Hydration and serialization are implemented by `ReflectionMapper`. Canonical Proxy / Address sample: Method Description `static fromArray(array $data): static` Create an instance and hydrate public properties `toArray(): array` Export initialized public properties (nested DTOs recursively) `toJson(): string` Pretty-printed JSON with Unicode and slashes unescaped; throws `JsonException` on failure `static setLogger(LoggerInterface $logger): void` Override the logger used for validation failures `static resetLogger(): void` Clear the custom logger (tests / teardown) Only **public, non-static** properties participate in mapping. Private/protected fields are ignored by the mapper. `ReflectionMapper::hydrate($target, $data)` walks public properties: Missing keys or explicit `null` trigger the null fallback. Values are converted according to the property type. `#[ArrayOf]` post-processes list properties. Validation attributes run on the converted value. Failures are logged and collected; after the pass, a non-empty error map raises `ValidationException`. Declared type Accepted input `string` string only `int` int, or numeric string via `FILTER_VALIDATE_INT` `float` float, int, or numeric string via `FILTER_VALIDATE_FLOAT` `bool` bool, `0`/`1`, or boolean strings via `FILTER_VALIDATE_BOOLEAN` `array` array `object` object `mixed` / untyped anything Union and intersection property types are not supported and fail conversion. If the property type is a subclass of `AbstractReflection` and the input is an array, the mapper instantiates the nested class and hydrates it with a dotted path prefix (`address.city`, `locations.0.city`). If the input is already an instance of the declared type (or interface), it is accepted as-is. When a key is missing or the value is `null`: properties with a default value keep their default nullable properties without a usable value become `null` required non-nullable properties without a default record `is required` When conversion or validation fails for a **nullable** property, the mapper sets the property to `null` instead of adding that path to the thrown error map (the failure is still logged). `ArrayOf` is both a conversion hint for the mapper and a `ValidationRule`. During conversion, the property value must be a **list** (`array_is_list`). Each element is converted to the declared type (builtin or nested `AbstractReflection`). Associative arrays fail with `must be a list`. Element failures appear as `ids.1`, `locations.0.city`, and so on. `toArray()` includes only initialized public properties. Nested `AbstractReflection` instances are expanded recursively. Plain arrays are walked element by element. `toJson()` encodes `toArray()` with: `JSON_THROW_ON_ERROR` `JSON_UNESCAPED_UNICODE` `JSON_PRETTY_PRINT` `JSON_UNESCAPED_SLASHES` `JSON_INVALID_UTF8_SUBSTITUTE` By default `AbstractReflection` uses an `Analog\\Logger`. Call `setLogger()` to capture validation failures in tests or application logging: Each failure is logged at error level with context keys `class`, `property` (dotted path), `expected`, and `actual_type`. You can hydrate an existing object without `fromArray()`: An optional second constructor argument accepts a custom `PropertyValidator`.","Public/Protected свойства Методы `__construct(string $type)` `validate(mixed $value): ?string` **Описание:** Атрибут «список элементов типа T». В `ReflectionMapper` управляет конверсией элементов; как `ValidationRule` проверяет list и типы. Repeatable. **Namespace:** `Devcraft\\Attributes` **Target:** `Attribute::TARGET_PROPERTY | Attribute::IS_REPEATABLE` **Implements:** ValidationRule **С версии:** 1.0.0 **См. также:** ReflectionMapper Гайд: Reflection mapper Гайд: валидация Свойство Тип Описание `$type` `string` Builtin (`string`, `int`, …) или FQCN класса/интерфейса **Параметры:** Параметр Тип Описание `$type` `string` Builtin (`string`, `int`, …) или FQCN класса/интерфейса **Описание:** `null` проходит. Не list → `must be a list of <type>`. Элемент не соответствует типу → то же сообщение. **Параметры:** Параметр Тип Описание `$value` `mixed` Проверяемое значение **Возвращает:** `string\\|null` Встроенные: `mixed`, `string`, `int`/`integer`, `float`/`double`, `bool`/`boolean`, `array`, `object`. Иначе — `instanceof`.","Public свойства Методы `withPostData(): self` `withHeader(): self` `withFormData(): self` `withMultipart(): self` `build(): self` **Описание:** Тело запроса: JSON, form, multipart, raw body, headers. За один запрос допускается только один тип тела (`postData` / `formData` / `multipart`). **Namespace:** `Devcraft\\Webshare\\Entities` **Extends:** `Devcraft\\Abstracts\\AbstractReflection` (dev-tools) **С версии:** 1.0.0 **См. также:** AbstractRequest Client Свойство Тип Описание `$header` `array` HTTP-заголовки тела. По умолчанию: `[]`. `$body` `?string` Raw body после `build()`. По умолчанию: `NULL`. `$postData` `array` JSON payload. По умолчанию: `[]`. `$formData` `array` Form-urlencoded поля. По умолчанию: `[]`. `$multipart` `array` Multipart части. По умолчанию: `[]`. **Описание:** Добавить поле в JSON body. **Параметры:** Параметр Тип Описание `$key` `string` Имя поля. `$value` `mixed` Значение. **Возвращает:** `self` **Описание:** Добавить HTTP-заголовок. **Параметры:** Параметр Тип Описание `$key` `string` Имя заголовка. `$value` `mixed` Значение. **Возвращает:** `self` **Описание:** Добавить поле form-urlencoded тела. **Параметры:** Параметр Тип Описание `$key` `string` Имя поля. `$value` `mixed` Значение. **Возвращает:** `self` **Описание:** Добавить часть multipart тела. **Параметры:** Параметр Тип Описание `$key` `string` Имя части. `$value` `mixed` Содержимое. **Возвращает:** `self` **Описание:** Подготовить headers и raw body перед отправкой (`Client::send` вызывает автоматически). **Возвращает:** `self` **Исключения:** `JsonException`","Public свойства Методы `getConnectionString(): string` **Описание:** Один прокси из списка; getConnectionString (backbone/direct). **Namespace:** `Devcraft\\Webshare\\Entities` **Extends:** `Devcraft\\Abstracts\\AbstractReflection` (dev-tools) **С версии:** 1.0.0 **См. также:** ProxyRequest Гайд: proxies Свойство Тип Описание `$id` `?string` Идентификатор. По умолчанию: `NULL`. `$username` `?string` Логин прокси. По умолчанию: `NULL`. `$password` `?string` Пароль прокси. По умолчанию: `NULL`. `$proxy_address` `?string` Адрес прокси. По умолчанию: `NULL`. `$port` `?int` Порт. По умолчанию: `NULL`. `$valid` `?bool` Валидность прокси. По умолчанию: `NULL`. `$last_verification` `?string` Последняя проверка. По умолчанию: `NULL`. `$country_code` `?string` Код страны. По умолчанию: `NULL`. `$city_name` `?string` Город. По умолчанию: `NULL`. `$asn_name` `?string` ASN имя. По умолчанию: `NULL`. `$asn_number` `?int` ASN номер. По умолчанию: `NULL`. `$high_country_confidence` `?bool` Высокая уверенность geo. По умолчанию: `NULL`. `$created_at` `?string` Дата создания. По умолчанию: `NULL`. **Описание:** Строка подключения backbone (`p.webshare.io`) или direct. **Параметры:** Параметр Тип Описание `$backbone` `bool` `true` — BackboneConnection, `false` — DirectConnection. По умолчанию: `false`. `$session` `?string` Session/rotate параметр backbone username. По умолчанию: `NULL`. `$city` `?string` City параметр backbone. По умолчанию: `NULL`. **Возвращает:** `string`","Public свойства Методы `getColumnVal(string $name): string\\|int\\|null\\|\\DateTimeImmutable` **Описание:** Одна заявка в очереди модерации. Таблица `{prefix}_tags_add` создаётся Cycle ORM по этой модели при первом обращении к модулю в админке. **Namespace:** `DevCraft\\Modules\\TagsAdd\\Models` **С версии:** 200.3.1 **См. также:** SuggestService, ModerationService Role Cycle: `tag_suggestion`. Репозиторий: `TagSuggestionRepository`. Индексы: `news_id`, `date`. Свойство Тип Описание `$news_id` `int` Новость. По умолчанию: `0` `$user_id` `int` Автор предложения; `0` — гость. По умолчанию: `0` `$tags` `string` Теги через запятую `$date` `\\DateTimeImmutable` Когда предложили `id` и служебные поля даты — у `AbstractEntity`. Чтение колонки по имени для таблиц админки (`id`, `news_id`, `user_id`, `tags`, `date`).","Public свойства **Описание:** SubUserList **Namespace:** `Devcraft\\Webshare\\Responses` **Extends:** PaginatedResponse **С версии:** 1.0.0 **См. также:** PaginatedResponse Свойство Тип Описание `$results` `array` Элементы текущей страницы. По умолчанию: `[]`.","Public свойства **Описание:** SubUser **Namespace:** `Devcraft\\Webshare\\Entities` **Extends:** `Devcraft\\Abstracts\\AbstractReflection` (dev-tools) **С версии:** 1.0.0 Свойство Тип Описание `$id` `?int` Идентификатор. По умолчанию: `NULL`. `$label` `?string` Метка. По умолчанию: `NULL`. `$proxy_countries` `mixed` По умолчанию: `NULL`. `$proxy_limit` `?float` По умолчанию: `NULL`. `$max_thread_count` `?int` По умолчанию: `NULL`. `$aggregate_stats` `array` По умолчанию: `[]`. `$created_at` `?string` Дата создания. По у